      en: ["A segment of the 600-kilometer inland waterway along the eastern coast.", "Constructed during the colonial era to bypass the dangerous Indian Ocean.", "Links a continuous series of natural coastal lakes and lagoons.", "Serves as the absolute economic lifeline for isolated coastal villages.", "Navigated constantly by traditional pirogues and large wooden cargo barges.", "Facilitates the vital transport of agricultural goods like bananas and coffee."]
